    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "grafana",
        "uid": "-- Grafana --"
      },
      "description": "How to read this dashboard and what it is not.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 16,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "markdown",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "**Estimated charges, not the invoice.** AWS publishes `AWS/Billing` `EstimatedCharges` to CloudWatch in **us-east-1** a few times a day (~every 6 hours). Values are month-to-date USD and reset each billing cycle. They do not include tax, credits, or a per-resource/tag split.\n\n**Empty panels?** Enable **Receive CloudWatch Billing Alerts** once in [Billing preferences](https://console.aws.amazon.com/costmanagement/) (root / billing-access IAM). Metrics appear in us-east-1 after ~15 minutes. Collection cannot be turned back off.\n\nIAM already has CloudWatch metric read; no extra keys or datasources.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "How to read this",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "cloudwatch",
        "uid": "cloudwatch"
      },
      "description": "SEARCH over AWS/Billing EstimatedCharges by ServiceName. Discovers whatever services are billing this cycle (CloudFront, S3, Route53, CloudWatch, …).",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 15,
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true,
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "none"
            }
          },
          "decimals": 2,
          "unit": "currencyUSD"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 12,
        "w": 16,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "id": 3,
      "options": {
